{"name":"Pony","hex":"#c6aa81","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Pony","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Ellipsis of Pony International, an American brand of athletic gear.","Ellipsis of My Little Pony, a cartoon media-franchise based on anthropomorphic equines."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An athletic shoe or other piece of athletic gear of an American-based brand of that name."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Pony"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pony","blocks":[{"text":"A pony is a type of small horse, usually under a specific height at full maturity. Ponies often have thicker coats, manes and tails, compared to larger horses, and proportionally shorter legs, wider barrels, heavier bone, thicker necks and shorter heads. In modern use, breed registries and horse shows may define a pony as measuring at the withers below a certain height; height limits varying from about 14 hands to 14.3 hands. Some distinguish between horse or pony based on its breed or phenotype, regardless of its height. The word pony derives from the old French poulenet, a diminutive of poulain meaning foal, a young, immature horse. A full-sized horse may sometimes be called a pony as a term of endearment."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Gracie-rhs2005.jpg/330px-Gracie-rhs2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pony","wikidata":"Q188828"},{"title":"Pony (Ginuwine song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Pony\" is a song by American singer and songwriter Ginuwine, released in July 1996, by 550 and Epic Records, as the debut single from his first album, Ginuwine... the Bachelor (1996). Ginuwine co-wrote the song with Swing Mob associates Static Major and Timbaland; the latter made his breakthrough as a producer with the song. Upon its release, the song was met with acclaim from music critics, and it peaked at number six on the US Billboard Hot 100 and number one on the Billboard Hot R&B Singles chart. The accompanying music video was directed by Michael Lucero."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/37/Ginuwine_-_Pony.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pony_(Ginuwine_song)","wikidata":"Q7228435"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Shetland_Pony_in_Harness_and_Cart.gif/500px-Shetland_Pony_in_Harness_and_Cart.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Shetland_Pony_in_Harness_and_Cart.gif/1280px-Shetland_Pony_in_Harness_and_Cart.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Shetland_Pony_in_Harness_and_Cart.gif/500px-Shetland_Pony_in_Harness_and_Cart.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Shetland pony shown in harness","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShetland_Pony_in_Harness_and_Cart.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/SackOTatersPony.jpg/330px-SackOTatersPony.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/SackOTatersPony.jpg/330px-SackOTatersPony.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A pony foal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASackOTatersPony.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Shetlands_in_Belgium.jpg/330px-Shetlands_in_Belgium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Shetlands_in_Belgium.jpg/330px-Shetlands_in_Belgium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":